{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall make the ephod.</b> Since the verse previously said ״חושן ואפוד ומעיל״ — 'the breastpiece, the ephod, and the robe' — it would have been fitting to put first and say, ״ועשית חושן משפט״ — 'and you shall make the breastpiece of judgment' — and afterward, ״ועשית את האפוד״ — 'and you shall make the ephod.'" "<b>And it is possible</b> to explain that He did so because the ephod is the principal element, for the breastpiece was beneath the ephod in the manner of a hem, and the ephod is the principal garment. Therefore the section put the ephod before the breastpiece in the making. And the reason it mentioned the breastpiece before the ephod was for the preeminence of the Explicit Name that is called Urim and Tumim, which were placed between the folds of the breastpiece." "<b>And know</b> that these garments — the breastpiece, the ephod, and the sash — were of wool and linen combined. And even though the Torah forbade all Israel כלאים (sha'atnez), to the priests it is permitted during the time of service, for the priests do not wear them except during the time of service. And this is what is written regarding the ephod: ״ועשו את האפוד זהב תכלת וארגמן ותולעת שני ושש משזר״; and it is written regarding the breastpiece: ״ועשית חושן משפט זהב תכלת וארגמן ותולעת שני ושש משזר״, and likewise regarding the sash. The תכלת is wool dyed like the color of the sky; ארגמן is wool dyed red; תולעת השני is wool dyed with the worm; and שש משזר — the שש is linen." "<b>And know</b> that the breastpiece and ephod were of five kinds, and the curtain of four kinds, and the pomegranates of the robe of three kinds. How so? Regarding the breastpiece of the ephod it is written: ״זהב תכלת וארגמן ותולעת שני ושש משזר״; and regarding the curtain it is written: ״ויעש את הפרוכת תכלת וארגמן ותולעת שני ושש משזר״; and regarding the pomegranates it is written: ״ויעשו על שולי המעיל רמוני תכלת וארגמן ותולעת שני משזר״ — שש is not mentioned there, for there were in the pomegranates only three kinds twined. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in tractate Yoma, chapter 'Ba La' (he enters): wherever שש is stated, each kind is doubled to six; משזר is eight — that is, משזר without שש, as in the pomegranates; the robe, twelve; the curtain, twenty-four; the breastpiece and ephod, twenty-eight. And the explanation of this is: the curtain, which is four kinds and in which שש is stated — each and every kind has six threads; so the curtain is twenty-four. The pomegranates, which have three kinds and in which שש is not stated — each kind has eight; so they are twenty-four — for they derive משזר from משזר of the curtain: just as משזר of the curtain, which is four kinds, is twenty-four, so too משזר of the pomegranates, which are three kinds, is twenty-four. The robe, twelve — for they derive תכלת from תכלת of the curtain: just as the curtain has six threads of תכלת, so too the robe; and it is written ״כליל״ and its meaning is גדיל (a cord), and a גדיל is no less than two; and so that yields twelve. The breastpiece and ephod, which have a fifth kind added to the rest, namely gold — it has twenty-eight threads: four kinds, six each, that is twenty-four; gold is the fifth kind — and one cannot say of it that it is six, for it is written concerning it (Exodus 39:3): ״וקצץ פתילים״, and Rashi of blessed memory explained there in tractate Yoma: פתילים — two, and when he comes to cut, they are four; if so, the breastpiece and ephod are twenty-eight threads."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {3 "Regarding the chapter citation: the rabbinic discussion of thread counts appears in Yoma 71b–72a, chapter 'Ba La' (הבא לו). The verse 'וקצץ פתילים' is Exodus 39:3; the printed citation 'שמות לג' appears to be a corruption or shorthand for ל״ג:׳."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:15.781682861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}